if (!pdev) {
    pr_warn("%s: failed to find ocram device!\n", __func__);
    ret = -ENODEV;
    goto put_node;
}
```
Reason:
The absence of a `put_device()` call after successfully finding the device with `of_find_device_by_node()` means that if an error occurs later in the function, the reference to the device is not released, leading to potential memory leaks or resource mismanagement.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
put_device:
    put_device(&pdev->dev);
```
Reason:
The addition of the `put_device(&pdev->dev);` call ensures that the device reference is properly released when an error occurs after the device has been successfully found, preventing memory leaks and ensuring proper resource management.

